ches the flour (up to 6)`),Q(1,`how many more: some sugar is on already (within 10)`),Q(1,`too much sugar: take spoons off until it is level (within 10)`),Q(1,`is it level? one bag the same as two (4 + 3 and 7)`),Q(2,`two bags make it: 8 + 6 balances 10 + 4 (within 20)`),Q(2,`two jars the same: which pair balances 10? (halves and doubles)`),Q(2,`tens and ones: bags of ten, then spoons (two digits to 49)`),Q(3,`bags by their number: 3 bags of 4 balance 12 (equal groups)`),Q(3,`a mystery jar: a jar and 5 balance 12, how many in the jar?`,!1),Q(3,`which side is heavier, without counting (27 + 15 and 27 + 16)`,!1),Q(4,`two weighings: two kinds of jar, found one after the other`,!1)]},{id:`spell-word`,subject:`writing`,name:`Spelling a word by its sounds`,friend:`kitty`,rungs:[Q(1,`short vowels, one letter for each sound (milk, salt, bun)`),Q(1,`two letters, one sound: ch, sh and doubles (egg, cherry, shells)`),Q(1,`long vowels: a vowel team or a quiet e (cheese, cream)`),Q(2,`r-vowels and -le (pepper, custard, sprinkles)`),Q(2,`c before e says s (rice)`),Q(2,`endings for more than one: -s, -ies (cherries, eggs, buns)`),Q(3,`sound-alikes: the meaning picks the spelling (flour, sugar)`,!1),Q(3,`long words, one beat at a time (spaghetti, pepperoni)`,!1)]},{id:`swap-letter`,subject:`reading`,name:`Change one letter, make a new word (the fridge magnets)`,friend:`kitty`,rungs:[Q(1,`the first letter (can, pan; dot, pot; bin, pin)`),Q(1,`a letter in the middle or at the end (pop, pot; pen, pin)`),Q(2,`letter pairs: ow on one magnet (bell, bowl); ea, one sound (pea, tea)`),Q(2,`two changes in a row, a thing at every step (top, pop, pot)`),Q(2,`add a letter, or take one off (owl, bowl; spot, pot; boats, oats)`),Q(2,`a quiet e at the end (cap, cape; pin, pine)`,!1),Q(3,`longer chains (pear, bear, beak, bean)`,!1)]},{id:`fix-sentence`,subject:`writing`,name:`Fixing a sentence (the café board comes true)`,friend:`kitty`,rungs:[Q(1,`a big letter at the start and a stop at the end`),Q