 by twos from its neighbours`),Q(2,`numbers past 100, a door without its number`),Q(3,`a little map: "the second street on the left"`,!1),Q(3,`two stops, and the shortest way`,!1)]},{id:`word-parts`,subject:`language`,name:`Word parts: un and re on the front of a word (the word stickers)`,friend:`kitty`,rungs:[Q(1,`un undoes: unwrap, unlock, uncover (one sticker roll)`),Q(2,`re does it again, beside un: refill, reheat, rewrap`),Q(2,`a note asks for it: read the word with its sticker and take it apart`),Q(2,`back stickers: -ful and -less (spoonful, seedless)`,!1),Q(3,`pre- and mis- (preheat, mismatch); two stickers on one word (unwrapped, refilled)`,!1),Q(3,`words a sticker cannot take (unheat, refun)`,!1)]},{id:`calendar`,subject:`time-money`,name:`Finding a day on the calendar (booking a party)`,friend:`chick`,rungs:[Q(1,`today and tomorrow, today ringed in gold`),Q(1,`a date by its number ("on the 21st")`),Q(2,`the coming day of the week ("on Saturday")`),Q(2,`counting on from today: in three days; in one week is one row down`),Q(2,`in two weeks; a week from tomorrow`),Q(3,`across the end of the month, on the next page`,!1),Q(3,`the second Tuesday of next month`,!1)]},{id:`plan-back`,subject:`time-money`,name:`Planning back from a time (when do we start?)`,friend:`chick`,known:!0,rungs:[Q(1,`one job of an hour, guests on the hour`),Q(1,`two jobs of half an hour each`),Q(2,`three jobs in quarter hours`),Q(2,`three jobs in five minutes`),Q(3,`guests at any five minutes: the start crosses the hour`),Q(3,`two cakes at once, or a rest between jobs`,!1)]},{id:`cake-words`,subject:`writing`,name:`Writing on a cake: the wish that fits, names, marks`,friend:`kitty`,rungs:[Q(1,`the wish that fits why the cake is for them, and a name starts with a big letter`),Q(1,`the wish word by word: words that look alike (well, will; soon, spoon)`),Q(2,`the name sound by sound, its first letter big (Frog, Chick, Bunny)`),Q(2,`the comma before the name, and the mark at the end of a wish`),Q(2,`whose day: the little mark and an s (Valentine's Day)`),Q(3,`words that sound the same: to, two, too; your, you're`),Q(3,`a longer wish, its words put in order (Happy 7th Birthday)`),Q(4,`a wish of their own, letter by letter, which Kitty reads out`,!1)]},{id:`read-note`,subject:`reading`,name:`Reading a guest's note`,friend:`kitty`,rungs:[Q(1,`one short sentence: a numeral or "no", one food word that can be sounded out`),Q(1,`number words (three, seven), and longer words that can be sounded out (candles, pickles)`),Q(1,`two parts in order: first this, then that`),Q(2,`little words that change it: don't, only, all but`),Q(2,`how much (a little, lots of), and harder food words (pepper, olives)`),Q(2,`a note that doesn't say it straight: it's my birthday, I am 7`),Q(3,`three sentences: find the one that says what to do`),Q(4,`if there is mint, add mint; if not, add a cherry`,!1)]},{id:`es-order`,subject:`spanish`,name:`Understanding Pengy in Spanish`,friend:`pengy`,oneRungADay:!0,steady:!0,rungs:[Q(1,`numbers 2 to 5 by ear, the food shown (tres cerezas)`),Q(1,`numbers 6 to 10 by ear, the food shown`),Q(1,`the food word by ear (cerezas, queso)`),Q(1,`number and food word, both by ear`),Q(1,`colors: the topping by its color (rojo, verde)`),Q(2,`sin: leave one off (sin queso)`),Q(2,`numbers 11 to 15 with a food (doce cerezas)`),Q(2,`me gusta, no me gusta`,!1),Q(2,`a kitchen word before its step (corta, mezcla, hornea)`,!1),Q(3,`two foods and "sin" in one order`,!1),Q(4,`answer Pengy: he asks, a choice is tapped, he says it in Spanish`,!1)]},{id:`compare-numbers`,subject:`maths`,name:`Comparing and ordering numbers`,friend:`frog`,rungs:[Q(1,`three tickets up to 10: the smallest came first (on the number line)`),Q(1,`10 to 30, a turned-around pair (12 and 21): tens first`),Q(1,`any two-digit numbers, where the ones mislead (41 and 29)`),Q(1,`three two-digit tickets in order, first to last`),Q(1,`now serving 47: who is next? One more, not ten more`),Q(2,`three-digit 